      "updated": 1785954786645,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5) Keep clock fair despite uneven latency?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5) Keep clock fair despite uneven latency?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lFrfEgJdnjcSI8qSnKzKd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1118.4922137801668,
      "y": 2087.610552454837,
      "width": 966.559326171875,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aP",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 683060010,
      "version": 31,
      "versionNonce": 741838314,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785954901857,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- The server stores each player's \"remaining_ms\" and the \"last_start_timestamp\"\nof when their clock started, reads from a monotonic clock, and subtracts elapsed time on demand. \nThe only writes happen on a move.\n- The actual work is compensating for latency. The server continuously measures round-trip time \nto each client with WebSocket ping/pong frames,\n independent of moves since a player might think for 30 seconds between them. \nIt keeps a rolling median rather than a mean, \nso one bad spike doesn't skew it. What it credits back is the full \"median_rtt\"\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- The server stores each player's \"remaining_ms\" and the \"last_start_timestamp\"\nof when their clock started, reads from a monotonic clock, and subtracts elapsed time on demand. \nThe only writes happen on a move.\n- The actual work is compensating for latency. The server continuously measures round-trip time \nto each client with WebSocket ping/pong frames,\n independent of moves since a player might think for 30 seconds between them. \nIt keeps a rolling median rather than a mean, \nso one bad spike doesn't skew it. What it credits back is the full \"median_rtt\"\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Pi6eowlP5iFl13qBCoQJb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1120.3682979651526,
      "y": 2317.3662415001363,
      "width": 374.19970703125,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
